# One shared scale: `ν Antiprism.SquareAntiprism.polyhedron`

`prismSquareAntiprism_nu_shared_list`: **every system of `prismSquareAntiprism_nu_roots_list` has its one root at the scale
`ν Antiprism.SquareAntiprism.polyhedron`** (`PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq`, `Modules/System/PolyRootEq.lean`): it is the one system. `prismSquareAntiprism_nu_reps_list`:
the same for the same system, and `prismSquareAntiprism_nu_reps` the statement in Mathlib's terms alone (`IsPolyRootEq`):
`ν Antiprism.SquareAntiprism.polyhedron` is the first coordinate of the root of each of these systems, each with exactly one root in its
box; it implies `IsPolyRootMax` (`IsPolyRootEq.isPolyRootMax`). There is one system (`PolynomialSystem.IsRootMax.isRootEq_singleton`).
Generated by `lean/scripts/exact_n.py` from the theorems of `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandPrismSquareAntiprism`, `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandPrismSquareAntiprism.Exact` and
`Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandPrismSquareAntiprism.Roots`, which it does not change.
-/

